From 2dcc66f2d606ccfb29daf4dfd7e3a9b942c3153c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 13:28:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(qos): flush stale flow-cache entries when QoS is disabled

Disabling QoS (qos_enable=0; restart_qos) tore down tc + iptables via
stop_iQos()/del_iQosRules() but never flushed the Broadcom flow
accelerator, leaving previously-offloaded flows with stale dstentry
refs. Result: the kernel spammed "blog_get_dstentry_by_id: N callbacks
suppressed" until a reboot. The enable path goes through fc_fini()
(fc disable + flush), but the disable path (IS_NON_AQOS() false ->
fc_disable=0) only ran fc_init() = fc enable, never a flush.

Add an HND-guarded `fc flush` after del_iQosRules() in the qos STOP
branch so the accelerator is cleared on disable, no reboot needed.
The web-GUI QoS toggle hits this same restart_qos path, so downstream
users are covered too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/services.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/services.c b/release/src/router/rc/services.c
index 674f28e508..cb2e91941c 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/services.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/services.c
@@ -18479,6 +18479,9 @@ check_ddr_done:
 			stop_dpi_engine_service(0);
 #endif
 			del_iQosRules();
+#ifdef HND_ROUTER
+			eval("fc", "flush");	// flush stale offloaded flows on QoS disable; fixes blog_get_dstentry_by_id spam (no reboot needed)
+#endif
 		}
 		if(action & RC_SERVICE_START) {
 #if defined(RTCONFIG_QCA) || \
